#%PAM-1.0
# Unlocking the WhiteRose lock screen with a fingerprint (fprintd), asked at
# the same time as the password (shell/pam/whiterose-lock), not instead of
# it. A missing reader or no enrolled fingers fails at once, and the lock
# screen just doesn't offer it. Packages install this as
# /etc/pam.d/whiterose-fingerprint.
auth required pam_fprintd.so max-tries=3 timeout=30
